LICENSE -- native/3rdparty/face/  (buffalo_l family face weights)

This file records the license posture of the two ONNX weights shipped in
native\3rdparty\face\bin\ :
    detection.onnx   = SCRFD-10GF   (insightface file name det_10g.onnx)
    recognition.onnx = ArcFace w600k_r50 (insightface file name w600k_r50.onnx)

It is NOT a license grant by this project. The terms below are quoted verbatim
from the upstream project that produced the weights. The upstream ships no
standalone LICENSE blob for these weights (HuggingFace cardData of
immich-app/buffalo_l says license=other / license_name=insightface and points at
the python-package License section), which is why this file is a quoted record
rather than a copied license text.

Upstream project: DeepInsight InsightFace
  license_link (from the HuggingFace model card metadata, retrieved 2026-10-15):
    https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface/tree/master/python-package#license
  Model source as recorded by D:\lightalbum_ai\face_server.py line 4:
    https://hf-mirror.com/immich-app/buffalo_l
      detection/model.onnx    -> SCRFD-10GF       (~17 MB, detection + 5-point keypoints)
      recognition/model.onnx  -> ArcFace w600k_r50 (~174 MB, 512-d identity embedding)

Verbatim License section of the upstream python-package README
(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/deepinsight/insightface/master/python-package/README.md,
HTTP 200, retrieved 2026-10-15):

    The library code is released under the MIT License, for academic and
    commercial use. The pretrained models provided with this library are for
    non-commercial research only, whether downloaded automatically or manually.

Consequences for this repository:

  * Upstream library CODE: MIT -- academic and commercial use allowed.
  * The PRETRAINED WEIGHTS shipped in bin/: NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH ONLY.
    Nothing in this repository claims, or may be read as claiming, a
    commercial-use grant for detection.onnx or recognition.onnx.
  * Any commercial distribution of these weights requires separate authorization
    from the upstream model authors first.
  * ONNX Runtime (bin/onnxruntime.dll) is a separate dependency under the MIT
    License; see THIRD_PARTY-NOTICE.md section 2 for its verbatim text.

Provenance / integrity: native/fetch_ai.ps1 hard-checks this file, the NOTICE and
the two SHA-256 digests pinned above-in-the-NOTICE before any byte is placed in
bin\ (verify-before-land), and offers a -SelfTest mode that injects the counter-
examples (bad SHA, deleted LICENSE, missing source) to prove those checks bite.
